# DeckBorne — catalog of known-compatible Bloodborne mods.
#
# THIS FILE IS A LIST OF POINTERS, NOT MOD FILES. DeckBorne does not and must not
# redistribute mods:
#   * Nexus's File Submission Guidelines prohibit re-hosting another author's content
#     without their permission, and ToS §10 limits downloads to personal use.
#   * A mod like the Xbox UI pack is a REPACKED GAME ASSET (dvdroot_ps4/menu/
#     common.tpf.dcx), i.e. a derivative of copyrighted files. That is exactly why the
#     shadPS4 project hosts memory PATCHES (byte offsets — data about the game) but no
#     mods, and why the whole mod scene lives on Nexus instead of GitHub.
# Shipping a URL is fine. Shipping the file is not — unless the author says yes, in
# which case add a `bundled` note here and credit them.
#
# Nexus also requires a login even for manual browser downloads, so nothing here can be
# fetched automatically. The user downloads; DeckBorne applies.
#
# FORMAT — pipe-delimited, four fields:
#   id | display name | source url | install hint
#
#   id           the folder under payloads/mods/ the user extracts into. Stage 40 merges
#                payloads/mods/<id>/ over the game root, so the extracted tree must be
#                rooted the same way the game is (dvdroot_ps4/... at the top).
#   display name shown in stage 40's report
#   source url   where to get it
#   install hint one line, what the mod actually replaces
#
# Entries here are OPTIONAL and never required by a profile. Stage 40 reports which are
# present and which aren't; it never fails an install over a missing mod.

xbox-ui|Xbox (and Switch) UI prompts|https://www.nexusmods.com/bloodborne/mods/30|replaces dvdroot_ps4/menu/common.tpf.dcx — swaps PS4 face/shoulder glyphs for Xbox or Switch
kbm-ui|Keyboard and mouse UI prompts|https://www.nexusmods.com/bloodborne/mods/460|same slot as xbox-ui (menu/common.tpf.dcx) — pick one, not both
custom-fonts|Custom Font Sets|https://gamebanana.com/mods/544026|drops a menu/ folder into dvdroot_ps4 — GameBanana, no login required; the Comic Sans set is an unmistakable "did my mod pipeline work" test
# vertex-explosion-fix is NOT cosmetic and NOT optional-in-spirit: it is the prerequisite
# for any FPS++ frame-rate patch. Confirmed 2026-07-19 that "30 FPS++" alone causes the
# vertex-explosion artifacting, and that this mod fixes it — `chocolate` ran the full patch
# set with the mod applied and the artifacting did not return. `deckborne` therefore ships
# "30 FPS++" AND a hard dependency on this mod.
#
# ⚠ IT IS STILL NOT BUNDLED, and that is a deliberate decision (2026-07-20). The author gave
# permission to redistribute, which clears the Nexus re-hosting rule — but not the second
# blocker in the header: the 144 fg_a_*.partsbnd.dcx files are repacked FromSoftware model
# files, and the author cannot license assets that aren't theirs. So the user downloads it,
# same as every other mod here. Do not "helpfully" add it to a release zip.
# NB it ships rooted at parts/, not at the game root — the "modloader friendly" packaging
# maps its root to dvdroot_ps4. That USED to need hand re-rooting; stage 40's placement
# resolver now works the depth out on its own, so extract it as-is and leave it alone.
vertex-explosion-fix|Vertex Explosion fix (required for FPS++ patches)|https://www.nexusmods.com/bloodborne/mods/109|replaces 144 dvdroot_ps4/parts/fg_a_*.partsbnd.dcx model files — fixes the geometry explosion that FPS++ patches cause
